  "statement": "Find a closed formula for $\\\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r\\\\,2^{r-1}$ and verify it for $n=3$.",
  "solution": "For $|x|\\\\neq 1$, $\\\\sum_{r=1}^{n}rx^{r-1}=\\\\tfrac{1-(n+1)x^{n}+nx^{n+1}}{(1-x)^{2}}$. With $x=2$: denominator $1$, numerator $1-(n+1)2^{n}+n\\\\cdot2^{n+1}=1+2^{n}(-n-1+2n)=1+(n-1)2^{n}$. So the sum is $1+(n-1)2^{n}$. For $n=3$: $1+2\\\\cdot 8=17$, and $1\\\\cdot1+2\\\\cdot2+3\\\\cdot4=1+4+12=17$.",
  "solutionStatus": "full",
  "hints": [
    "Differentiate $\\\\sum x^{r}=\\\\tfrac{x(1-x^{n})}{1-x}$ with respect to $x$.",
    "Set $x=2$ at the end."
  ],
